<header><p class="st-kicker">other · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Provisional Government of Hawaii</h1><p class="st-meta">1893 CE – 1894 CE · capital Honolulu</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The government set up by American and European businessmen after the overthrow of Queen Liliʻuokalani in 1893, created to secure annexation by the United States.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In January 1893 Queen Liliʻuokalani proposed a new constitution to restore royal power. A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/committee-of-safety-hawaii">Committee of Safety</a> led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorrin-a-thurston">Lorrin A. Thurston</a>, made up mostly of American <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> interests, seized government buildings on 17 January, while the US minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-l-stevens">John L. Stevens</a> landed marines from USS <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a>. The queen yielded under protest to the superior force of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a>, and the committee proclaimed a provisional government.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanford-b-dole">Sanford B. Dole</a> headed an executive council, with an advisory council of the overthrow's supporters, and ruled without elections, requiring officials to swear loyalty. Its single goal was annexation, and it quickly sent a treaty to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/washington-dc">Washington</a>. It kept the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-hawaii">Kingdom of Hawaii</a>'s laws and bureaucracy largely in place.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grover-cleveland">Grover Cleveland</a> withdrew the treaty and, after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/blount-report">Blount Report</a> found American complicity, asked for the queen's restoration. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanford-b-dole">Dole</a> refused. To secure itself until annexation became possible, the government proclaimed the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-hawaii">Republic of Hawaii</a> on 4 July 1894. The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a> formally apologised for the overthrow in 1993.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/provisional-government-of-hawaii.jpg" alt="Provisional Government of Hawaii" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: FOTW, Clay Moss (PNG), Government of the Republic of Hawaii · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Hawaii_(1896).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1893 CE – 1894 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Honolulu</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Sanford B. Dole</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Protestantism, Hawaiian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English, Hawaiian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-states">United States</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Provisional Government of the Hawaiian Islands</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1894&amp;focus=provisional-government-of-hawaii" aria-label="Provisional Government of Hawaii on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="439 1390 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Provisional Government of Hawaii lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M759 1646L759 1646M759 1646L759 1646"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M759 1646h0M759 1646h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M759 1646h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M759 1646h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Honolulu. <a href="/atlas?year=1894&amp;focus=provisional-government-of-hawaii">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
